  "result": "Subcommands now get their own section of `default_map` instead of the parent's whole map. Before the fix, `{\"runserver\": {\"port\": 5000}}` was passed down unchanged, so `runserver` looked for `port` at the top level and never found it.\n\nThe fix is one line in `Context.__init__` in `src/click/core.py`. It now reads `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`, which matches what `docs/commands.md` describes.\n\nI ran `tests/test_defaults.py`, `tests/test_context.py` and `tests/test_options.py` and all 716 tests pass. I didn't add a test for the nested subcommand case and didn't run the rest of the suite.",
